= Technology Option  [TECH-nn] =

//An available or emerging capability considered for the System — including options considered and rejected, so the rationale is a selection rather than a justification.//

**Report Format:** §1.3 Technology

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|Stable identifier, unique within this entity type (e.g. TECH-01, TECH-02…).
|Name|A short, human-readable label for this instance.
|Status|Not Started / In Progress / Under Review / In Evaluation / Finalized.
|Evidence basis|How this knowledge was obtained — direct observation, interview, literature, secondary data, or proxy informant — flagged as provisional where it rests on anything other than direct contact with the Stakeholder group it describes. For a Measure or Evaluation Method, cite existing use in a validation study or authoritative literature (e.g. a validated-instrument source or textbook) instead.
|Category|AI/ICT, Social Robot, sensing, or other.
|Capabilities|what it can do that is relevant here.
|Limitations|what it cannot do, and where it degrades.
|Maturity and feasibility|technical readiness within this project's real constraints.
|Failure and fallback behaviour|what happens when it fails or is unavailable.
|Benefits|which Goals or Human Values it serves, by ID.
|Drawbacks|including which Value Tension it strains, by ID.
|Selected or rejected|and, if rejected, the reason — a rejected option is still Foundation knowledge.

== Graph edges ==

enables → (Specification-phase) Function; addresses → Goal / Human Value; strains → Value Tension.